# MOTHER3 (AGB-A3UJ): the characters of the game's font by their numbers, as the script has them (16-bit, the
# low byte first). Kana follow a rule and are not listed (the script has it).
#
# The font is in the cartridge from 0xCE39FC: 11 rows of 16 bits a character, one bit a pixel, in the order of
# JIS X 0208 by row and cell: rows 1-8 (signs, digits, letters, kana; 94 numbers a row), then the NEC row 13
# (circled digits, units) at 752, then the kanji's rows 16-84 from 846. So a number n is the JIS character at
# row n//94+1 (below 752), row 13 (752-845), or row (n-846)//94+16 (from 846), its cell the remainder plus one;
# each was drawn from the cartridge and its order checked by eye at the rows' starts and ends, and the eleven
# read in play before agree with it but one: 00AC, a cell JIS leaves empty, which the game uses as a space.
# Numbers that are empty cells in JIS (and the font's few own pictures there) aren't listed.
